<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Laws</h1>
<p>Midgaard and Udgaard keep the law, each in its own lands; everywhere 
else, the King's Castle included, falls under Midgaard's law. The law 
protects every player who is in good standing, and many townsfolk: 
shopkeepers, guards and others marked as protected. Killing a protected 
character, or being caught stealing from one, is a crime.
</p><p><b>Self-defence.</b> Whoever attacks a protected character first, or 
casts a harmful spell at one, may be killed without crime while they stay 
in that room; so may a thief who is caught. Guards also treat evil 
creatures as fair game.
</p><p><b>Witnesses and accusing.</b> Everyone in the room who can see the deed 
witnesses the crime, and is told so. A protected townsperson who saw it 
walks to the captain and accuses you by themselves; a player must go to 
the captain of the city guard and accuse you there (see <a cmd='#'>Help Accuse</a>). 
A player's memory of a crime lasts two weeks.
</p><p><b>Your record.</b> Each accusation adds to your record: 3 for stealing, 
8 for murder. With any record at all you lose the protection of the law, 
and on 32 or more you are <b>wanted</b> (an outlaw): guards who see you 
arrest you. On 64 or more you are <b>wanted dead</b>: there is a reward on 
your head, and guards attack you on sight. Any accusation also puts a 
reward on your head, larger the higher your level and record. The board 
in the captain's office lists who is wanted.
</p><p><b>Arrest and jail.</b> A guard who arrests you puts you in handcuffs: you 
can do nothing but look and talk while you are led to the captain, unless 
you manage to <a cmd='#'>break</a> the cuffs (see <a cmd='#'>Help Break</a>), which makes you wanted 
dead. He 
locks your belongings away and puts you in jail for about an hour of real 
time. When you are released, you get your things back, that city's 
record against you is cleared, and you are under the law's protection 
again. Escape, and you are wanted dead.
</p><p><b>Paying for it.</b> When you die, all is forgiven: your record is wiped, 
the rewards on you are gone, and you are under the law's protection 
again. Your killer can cut the head off your corpse (see <a cmd='#'>Help 
Decapitate</a>) and bring it to the captain for the reward. But the 
witnesses still remember, and may accuse you again.
</p><p>Players may only kill one another if both have signed the Book of Blood, 
wanted or not (see <a cmd='#'>Help Book of Blood</a>).
</p><p><br />
